course: dictionary
lesson: 10527
title: Spotting a typo
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A typo is a small mistake when you type or print a word, such as a wrong or missing letter. «teh» instead of «the» is a typo.
explain: Typos are normal and do not mean you do not know the rule. «A typo is a typing mistake; a mistake doesn't always mean someone doesn't know the rule.» A typo is a slip of the fingers.
explain: Context helps you spot a typo. Read the sentence again and ask: does this word fit? In «see you at scool», the word is not right for the sentence, so the letters are probably a typo for school. Checking your writing for typos before you hand it in is a good habit.
fact: A typo is a small mistake in typing or printing.
fact: Typo is short for typing error, or typographical error.
fact: «teh» is a typo for «the».
fact: A typo is a typing mistake, not a sign that someone does not know the rule.
fact: Autocorrect can fix some typos, but it can also miss them, so check your work.
exercise: What is a typo? | *A small mistake in typing or printing | A long story told in a book | A kind of printer that makes loud noises
exercise: The word «teh» is written instead of «the». What is the typo? | *teh | of | the | instead
exercise: A book has 200 pages and there are 3 typos on each page. How many typos are there in total? | *600 | 203 | 60 | 2003
test: Which word is short for typographical error? | tip | *typo | topic | typeface
test: Why is it fine to make a typo when you are typing quickly? | *A typo is a slip, and it does not always mean you don't know the rule | Typos show you cannot spell at all | Typos mean the whole text is wrong and must be thrown away
exam: In «see you at scool», which word is the typo? | at | see | *scool | you
